<h3>Why 100 % Declared‑Value Marine Transit Insurance Matters</h3>
<p>Marine transit insurance is the safety net that guards your car against loss, damage, or theft while it’s on the move—whether it’s by sea, rail, or road. A 100 % declared‑value policy means the insurer agrees to cover the full market value of the vehicle, not just a partial or limited sum.</p>
<p>This level of coverage is critical for high‑value cars, exotic models, or any vehicle where replacement costs are significant. By opting for a 100 % declared‑value policy, you eliminate the risk of under‑insurance and ensure that, in the unlikely event of an incident, you receive compensation that reflects the true worth of your vehicle.</p>

<p>In summary, the combination of a self‑attested RC photocopy, current PUC, valid insurance certificate, and an IBA‑approved consignment bilty forms the backbone of a legally compliant transport process in Sherkot.</p>
